  "title": "Combrisson-2024-neural-10.7554/elife.92938",
  "description": "This derivative dataset provides high-gamma power (50-100 Hz) computed from bipolar stereotactic EEG derivations in 16 patients with pharmaco-resistant epilepsy. The patients performed a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment conditions. Recordings cover four frontal regions: anterior insula, dorsolateral prefrontal cortex, lateral orbitofrontal cortex and ventromedial prefrontal cortex. The data were used to show dissociable reward and punishment subsystems using information-theoretic analyses. Raw iEEG is not included.",
  "methods_description": "Depth SEEG was recorded with a Micromed system at 512 or 1024 Hz. Bipolar derivations between adjacent grey-matter contacts were computed, and artifactual or pathological sites were removed. Gamma power (50-100 Hz) was estimated with a multitaper transform, down-sampled to 256 Hz, and time-locked to the outcome (-0.5 to 1.5 s). Trial-wise prediction errors came from a Q-learning model. Patients performed a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment cue pairs.",
